From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christer Solskogen <christer.solskogen@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] uae: keep one RAMBlock per mapped PPC region

ppc_cpu_map_memory_single() re-initialised a live MemoryRegion in place
when UAE remapped a region at the same address and size. That leaked the
old RAMBlock, which kept aliasing the same host memory. TCG keys
translated code by the RAMBlock that qemu_ram_addr_from_host() returns,
while guest stores dirty the RAMBlock of the current mapping, so writes
no longer invalidated translations. After a warm Amiga reset AmigaOS 4
loaded programs over memory that held earlier code and crashed (ISI/DSI
gurus).

Keep the region when its backing is unchanged, and otherwise unparent it
and add a new one so the old RAMBlock is released.
---
 uae/qemu-uae-cpu.c | 28 +++++++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/uae/qemu-uae-cpu.c b/uae/qemu-uae-cpu.c
index 589140b..571d4d9 100644
--- a/uae/qemu-uae-cpu.c
+++ b/uae/qemu-uae-cpu.c
@@ -270,19 +270,25 @@ static void ppc_cpu_map_memory_single(PPCMemoryRegion *r)
         if (mem->region == NULL)
             continue;
         if (mem->addr == r->start && mem->size == r->size) {
+            bool is_ram = memory_region_is_ram(mem->region);
+            if (r->memory ? (is_ram && memory_region_get_ram_ptr(mem->region) ==
+                             r->memory)
+                          : !is_ram) {
+                /* Same backing: keep the region and its RAMBlock. */
+                return;
+            }
+            /*
+             * Never re-initialise a live MemoryRegion in place: that leaks its
+             * RAMBlock, which keeps aliasing the same host memory. TCG then
+             * keys translated code by one RAMBlock while guest stores dirty
+             * the other, so self-modifying code (e.g. a program loaded over
+             * old code after a warm reboot) keeps running stale translations.
+             */
             uae_log("QEMU: region %02d replaced\n", i);
             memory_region_del_subregion(get_system_memory(), mem->region);
-            if (r->memory) {
-                memory_region_init_ram_ptr(mem->region, NULL, r->name, r->size,
-                                           r->memory);
-            } else {
-                memory_region_init_io(
-                    mem->region, NULL, &indirect_ops,
-                    (void *) (uintptr_t) r->start, r->name, r->size);
-            }
-            memory_region_add_subregion(
-                get_system_memory(), r->start, mem->region);
-            return;
+            object_unparent(OBJECT(mem->region));
+            mem->region = NULL;
+            break;
         }
     }
     ppc_cpu_map_add(r);
